{"subject":"Englisch","title":"Blue Line 1 – Unit 2 Vokabeln Teil 3 (S. 200–203)","key":"Blue Line 1 – Unit 2 (Vokabeln, Seite 200–203)\nAlphabet-Lied und Buchstaben: a [eɪ], e [i:], g [dʒi:], i [aɪ], j [dʒeɪ], y [waɪ], z [zed]\nReading corner / Film corner: trick, saxophone, lunch, Let's …, winner, Well done!, to make friends, chewing gum, jeans, circus, club\nAt school: assembly hall, playground, recording studio, cafeteria, sports hall, science lab, music room, art room, toilets\nBefehle: Sit down, please! Open your exercise books! Look at the board! Close the window! Put your hands up! Take out your pens!\nFächer: Geography, DT, Biology, German, Science, French, RE, IT, History, English, Physics, Art, Chemistry, Food Technology, Social Studies, PE, Textiles, Maths\nMy favourite subject is … I like … I don't like … It's / It isn't interesting.","vocab":[["funny","lustig; witzig"],["interesting","interessant"],["on Tuesday","am Dienstag"],["day","Tag"],["to spell","buchstabieren"],["like that","so"],["timetable","Stundenplan"],["registration","Überprüfung der Anwesenheit"],["boring","langweilig"],["difficult","schwierig"],["fun","Freude; Spaß"],["alphabet","Alphabet"],["Let's all go out and play.","Lasst uns alle rausgehen und spielen."],["Come over here and stand by me.","Komm her und stelle dich neben mich."],["Can you fly?","Kannst du fliegen?"],["all alone","ganz allein"],["but not","aber nicht"],["Now you're set to go ahead.","Jetzt bist du bereit, um weiterzumachen."],["trick","Trick; Streich"],["saxophone","Saxophon"],["lunch","Mittagessen"],["let's (= let us)","lass(t) uns"],["What's your talent?","Was ist dein Talent?"],["to see","sehen"],["winner","Gewinner; Gewinnerin"],["Well done!","Gut gemacht!"],["star","Star"],["to make friends","Freundschaften schließen"],["chewing gum","Kaugummi"],["jeans (pl)","Jeans"],["Alicia put it in there.","Alicia hat es dort hinein getan."],["film","Film"],["leaflet","Broschüre; Prospekt"],["club","Klub; Schul-AG"],["circus","Zirkus"],["I don't understand","ich verstehe nicht"],["assembly hall","Aula"],["recording studio","Tonstudio"],["sports hall","Sporthalle"],["science lab","Labor; Naturwissenschaftsraum"],["music room","Musikraum"],["art room","Kunstraum"],["toilets","Toiletten"],["to listen","zuhören"],["to play games","Spiele spielen"],["to drink","trinken"],["to play football","Fußball spielen"],["to do sport","Sport treiben"],["to do experiments","Experimente machen"],["to play music","Musik machen"],["to draw a picture","ein Bild malen"],["to go to the toilet","auf die Toilette gehen"],["Sit down, please!","Setzt euch bitte hin!"],["Open your exercise books!","Öffnet eure Übungshefte!"],["Look at the board!","Schaut an die Tafel!"],["Write on the board!","Schreibt an die Tafel!"],["Close the window!","Macht das Fenster zu!"],["Open the window!","Öffnet das Fenster!"],["Close the door!","Macht die Tür zu!"],["Open the door!","Öffnet die Tür!"],["Put your hands up!","Meldet euch!"],["Take out your pens!","Nehmt eure Stifte heraus!"],["Do exercise two.","Macht Aufgabe zwei."],["Talk to your partner.","Sprecht mit eurem Partner."],["Physics","Physik"],["Chemistry","Chemie"],["Food Technology","Ernährungslehre"],["Social Studies","Gesellschaftslehre"],["Textiles","Textilgestaltung"],["My favourite subject is …","Mein Lieblingsfach ist …"],["I like …","Ich mag …"],["I don't like …","Ich mag … nicht"],["It's / It isn't interesting.","Es ist / Es ist nicht interessant."],["OK","okay"],["easy","einfach"],["nice","nett; schön"]],"tasks":[{"type":"choice","q":"Welcher Buchstabe wird [eɪ] gesprochen?","options":["a","e","i"],"answer":"a","hint":"","explain":"a = [eɪ], e = [i:], i = [aɪ]."},{"type":"choice","q":"Welcher Buchstabe wird [dʒeɪ] gesprochen?","options":["j","g","k"],"answer":"j","hint":"","explain":"j = [dʒeɪ], g = [dʒi:], k = [keɪ]."},{"type":"choice","q":"Welcher Buchstabe wird [dʒi:] gesprochen?","options":["g","j","c"],"answer":"g","hint":"","explain":"g = [dʒi:]."},{"type":"choice","q":"Welcher Buchstabe wird [waɪ] gesprochen?","options":["y","w","i"],"answer":"y","hint":"","explain":"y = [waɪ]."},{"type":"choice","q":"Welcher Buchstabe wird [zed] gesprochen?","options":["z","s","x"],"answer":"z","hint":"","explain":"z = [zed] (britisch)."},{"type":"choice","q":"Welcher Buchstabe wird [i:] gesprochen?","options":["e","i","a"],"answer":"e","hint":"","explain":"e = [i:]."},{"type":"choice","q":"Welcher Buchstabe wird [aɪ] gesprochen?","options":["i","e","y"],"answer":"i","hint":"","explain":"i = [aɪ]."},{"type":"text","q":"Ergänze: «Can you ___ Monday? It's easy.» (buchstabieren)","answer":"spell","alt":[],"hint":"to spell","explain":"Can you spell Monday?"},{"type":"text","q":"Ergänze: «We have English ___ Tuesday.»","answer":"on","alt":[],"hint":"","explain":"on Tuesday = am Dienstag."},{"type":"text","q":"Ergänze: «Don't talk ___ that!» (so)","answer":"like","alt":[],"hint":"","explain":"like that = so."},{"type":"text","q":"Das Gegenteil von «boring» ist …","answer":"interesting","alt":[],"hint":"","explain":"boring ↔ interesting."},{"type":"text","q":"Das Gegenteil von «difficult» ist …","answer":"easy","alt":[],"hint":"","explain":"difficult ↔ easy."},{"type":"text","q":"Ergänze: «Geography is ___.» (Spaß)","answer":"fun","alt":[],"hint":"","explain":"Geography is fun."},{"type":"text","q":"Ergänze: «___ go to the talent show.» (Lasst uns)","answer":"Let's","alt":["let's","Lets"],"hint":"let us","explain":"Let's go to the talent show."},{"type":"text","q":"Ergänze: «Well ___!» (Gut gemacht!)","answer":"done","alt":[],"hint":"","explain":"Well done!"},{"type":"text","q":"Übersetze: «Ich verstehe nicht.»","answer":"I don't understand.","alt":["I don't understand","I do not understand"],"hint":"","explain":"I don't understand."},{"type":"text","q":"Ergänze: «to make ___» (Freundschaften schließen)","answer":"friends","alt":[],"hint":"","explain":"to make friends."},{"type":"text","q":"Ergänze: «No chewing ___ at school.» (Kaugum